      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm doing some reading on international relations stuff and was wondering... how do modern historians generally view the effectiveness of the UN in preventing major conflicts in the 21st century?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Generally, modern historical views are nuanced, often suggesting the UN has a mixed record in 21st-century conflict prevention. While the UN has been crucial in conflict *mitigation* and post-conflict stabilization, its power to *prevent* major state-level wars is often constrained by the political will and veto power of its most powerful members. Therefore, success is often seen in specific, targeted peace support and human rights advocacy rather than absolute conflict prevention.",
